From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Combray <combray@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:28:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Embedder API: expose top-level document identity

- Re-export PipelineId; WebView::active_document_id() reports the
  active top-level document as of the last history change.
- HistoryChanged, load-status and title messages carry the reporting
  document. New WebViewDelegate methods notify_document_load_status_changed
  and notify_document_title_changed receive every report with its
  document, so embedders can discard reports from replaced documents.
- WebView::evaluate_javascript_in_document() only runs a script if the
  given document is still active; otherwise DocumentNotFound.
- GlobalScope::evaluate_js_on_global returns DocumentNotFound instead
  of asserting can_run_script(). Embedder evaluations, WebDriver
  ExecuteScript and user scripts can all reach it after a navigation
  or an iframe deactivation; the assert took down the script thread
  and every WebView on it.
---
